# Kafka WSL + Windows Debugging

## 1. Kafka running?
ss -ltnp | grep 9092

## 2. Kafka internally working?
bin/kafka-topics.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --list

## 3. Windows can reach WSL Kafka?
PowerShell:
Test-NetConnection <WSL-IP> -Port 9092

## 4. Find WSL IP
wsl hostname -I

## 5. Kafka advertised address
config/server.properties

advertised.listeners=PLAINTEXT://<WSL-IP>:9092

## 6. Spring Boot
spring:
  kafka:
    bootstrap-servers: <WSL-IP>:9092

## Golden rule:
Kafka running != Kafka reachable by application.

Always check:
1. Kafka is running
2. Network is reachable
3. advertised.listeners is correct
4. Spring bootstrap-server is correct